@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+# v2 camera zoom tiers + node-vs-puck legibility rebalance
+
+**User directive (2026-08-23):** "after the last update with zoom and map in
+PP, now even zoomed in I can barely see the buildings, and the routers are big
+— the scale is all messed up. Default should be zoomed in, to see the buildings
+and the links, then an extra zoom in for the node/link click, then zoom out is
+just to see all the links and the job done across the map."
+
+## What ships
+
+- **Three-tier zoom model (A)** — the camera now has an explicit, non-overlapping
+  tier ladder with the RESTING HOME at the cluster default, not the whole-map fit:
+  - **Default (entry / run start / deselect / ESC):** `camera_set_default` —
+    2.0x (`DEFAULT_ZOOM`, new) centered on the **source cluster** (the
+    fixture's centroid — the first buildings + links the player meets).
+  - **Focus (node/link click):** unchanged 2.3x / 2.6x (`camera_set_selection`).
+  - **Out (whole-map backbone / job-done):** unchanged manual wheel-out floor
+    `CAM_ZOOM_MIN = 1.0` — the only way to the bird's-eye now.
+  - `camera_set_fit` is no longer a resting state: its three resting call sites
+    (boot via `start_run`, run reset, the deselect else-branch) now call
+    `camera_set_default`. ESC (`effect_cancel`) also homes to the default —
+    "return home" is the cluster now (a small reasoned extension of A: ESC
+    throwing the player to the whole-map bird's-eye would contradict the
+    directive; flagged for the review).
+  - **Pullback floor:** `camera_pullback_target`'s lower clamp is now
+    `DEFAULT_ZOOM` (2.0), not the 1.0 fit. **Documented tradeoff:** a district
+    seeded beyond the 2.0 viewport may sit at the edge (or stay out) rather
+    than forcing a full-out bird's-eye — the accepted behavior (the player
+    stays in the zoomed-in mindset; the whole-map view is only the manual
+    wheel-out). B1 (Perkins r2) is preserved: the target center still runs
+    through the bounds clamp at the target zoom, so the converged viewport
+    never leaves the world rect — but the floor no longer pins the world
+    center (that was the 1.0-fit contract, where the viewport was larger than
+    the world).
+- **Terminal blocks legible (B)** — `DUBLIN_NODE_BLOCK_L/W` 0.40/0.22 →
+  0.55/0.30 (world tiles): the street-aligned blocks were rendering ~3x
+  smaller than the pucks at the 2.0x default. Still street-aligned, sized
+  against the street layout (a 0.55-long block sits within a street lane;
+  the growth director's 5-tile attach radius keeps blocks well-separated).
+- **Router pucks reigned in (C)** — `sprite_puck_target`: base multiplier
+  1.15 → 1.05 AND the tier growth factor (`bbox[idx]/base`) is now CAPPED at
+  `PUCK_GROWTH_MAX = 1.30`. A high-tier puck stays just above a terminal
+  block instead of ~3x it; the tier ladder still reads (shipped puck ratios
+  top out at 1.27, inside the cap — the cap is the future-proof ceiling).
+  Pucks stay crisp (vectors, never softened). The puck rim/wash/ring in
+  `draw_router` already rode the single `dst` from `sprite_puck_target` —
+  one source, no change needed there.
+- **Sim untouched (ODN-1)** — camera + sprite sizing are presentation-only;
+  the core, the T1 hashes, and the replay gate do not see a byte.
+
+## Golden re-bless (deliberate, cause-documented)
+
+- **T1 hashes: unchanged** (48/48 green — the sim never saw this change).
+- **T2 pixels: re-blessed deliberately** — the puck footprint shrink (C) and
+  the Dublin terminal-block growth (B) shift every node-bearing frame; the
+  harness diff bundles confirmed the mismatches are exactly the puck/block
+  geometry (no other pixel drifted). Re-blessed via `tools/harness.sh save`.
+- **palcheck floors re-pinned where the puck shrink dropped pixel counts**
+  (e.g. the puck hardware-tone floor) — measured on the re-blessed frames,
+  keeping the crop/blit-canary job (a missing sprite still zeroes the count).
+
+## Verify
+
+- `odin test core` — green (261 tests, unchanged).
+- `odin test app/render` — green (81 tests; new pins: `DEFAULT_ZOOM` tier
+  ladder, `camera_cluster_center` fixture home, the pullback floor at
+  DEFAULT_ZOOM + the documented-tradeoff pins).
+- `odin test app` — green (43 tests; `camera_set_default_homes_on_the_source_cluster`,
+  the rail-on floor pin, the ESC-home leg now drives `camera_set_default`).
+- `tools/harness.sh run` — green after the re-bless.
+- `tools/ci-local.sh` — see the gate summary.
